---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Home" description="Ava Celeste — mature escort, available in RVA, to DC, to North Carolina and beyond.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Available in RVA, to DC, to North Carolina and beyond</p>
    <h1>Your <span class="accent-text">manic pixie dream</span> — calm, mature, alive girl.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">Mature escort. Available for outcall in the Richmond, VA area.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <blockquote class="pull-quote">A love affair, <em>sans</em> messy entanglements.</blockquote>

    <h2>Who do you want to meet?</h2>
    <p class="drop-cap">
      You want a companion who is pleasing to your eyes, pleasing to touch — anything but basic and bland.
      How about an all-natural, well-maintained beauty; with intelligence and quiet elegance; strong legs,
      firm bum; smooth, soft skin — who makes you feel welcome? Someone who can quote Monty Python, keep
      secrets, and drives a manual sports car.
    </p>

    <h2>Hi! I'm Ava.</h2>
    <p>
      An enabler of feelings for men who want a bit of spark in their life, to feel special again. A touch
      of romance without entanglements. The smart, safe way to have a fling.
    </p>
    <p>Instead of a parasocial relationship, have a <em>real</em> one.</p>
    <p>
      I don't pretend to be for everyone, because I know I lack mass appeal. (I'm the obscure band t-shirt
      of escorts.) So how do you know if I'm for you? Compatibility. That spark is <em>everything</em>,
      because a bad match is a bad time for both of us.
    </p>
    <p>
      My straightforwardness can be disconcerting. I'm frank to give you what you need to decide if we
      should meet. You can sample me for free through my blog and socials. (Soon, you'll have more options!)
    </p>
    <p>
      (I'm not the destination — just the door, and doors are meant to be opened.
      <a href="/me/">Read more →</a>)
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">Always</p>
    <h2>Quality Over Quantity</h2>
    <p><strong>What does quality mean to me? Extreme compatibility.</strong></p>
    <p>
      There are only a few things I take seriously. Safety is first. Compatibility is a close second —
      incompatibility leads to a bad time for everyone, while genuine compatibility feels like you're on
      a date, meeting someone you should have met years ago.
    </p>
    <p>
      I love that feeling. Isn't it the best? Nothing else compares. It can't be faked. It requires
      compatibility.
    </p>
    <p>
      That's why this site — and my blog — are so wordy: so we can find out if we're compatible before we
      ever meet. I don't want to <em>pretend</em> to like you, I want to <em>actually</em> like you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Compatible doesn't mean identical. You don't have to agree with everything I say, like everything I
      like, or think every decision I've made was the right one. If most of what I say resonates with you
      — that's ideal! All that's required is thinking you'd enjoy spending time with me.
    </p>
    <p>
      But if something here is a real turn-off — not a quirk, but a foundational clash for one of us —
      trust that. Go with your gut; it's not wrong. Yes, really: an escort is telling you to skip her if
      you don't actually like her. I can tell when the vibe's off, and I'd guess you can too. Why do that
      to each other?
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How It Starts</h2>
    <p>
      We start with cocktails — whether in Richmond or not. I'm travel-ready, including driving within
      reasonable distances.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>If you're ready, get in touch!</h2>
    <p>
      <a class="button" href="/contact/">Contact / Screening</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Or, curious who you'd actually be meeting? <a href="/me/">Read my introduction</a>.
      Wondering if we're a fit? <a href="/you/">See who I'm looking for</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 2rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.6rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .hero-sub {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .pull-quote {
    font-family: var(--font-header);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
    border-left: none;
    margin: 2rem auto;
    max-width: 32rem;
  }
  .cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 2rem 0;
  }
  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--near-black);
    color: var(--near-white);
    padding: 0.75em 1.5em;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
</style>
